agent.result_text:
The as-of view is in place, and all 4 tests in `e2e/specs/acceptance.spec.ts` pass with `bin/e2e`.

**On screen.** Next to the sheet's today there is now a date entry (`asof-date`), a set button (`asof-set`), a clear button (`asof-clear`), and `sheet-asof`, which shows the as-of date or nothing. The date belongs to that browser only. While it is set, every request from that screen carries an `X-As-Of` header. Other users don't send it, so they see the sheet as it is now. One visible effect: while an as-of date is set, the "Today" field shows the as-of date, because that date stands in for today in every figure.

**Changes are refused.** A new server check (`sheet/AsOfGuard.java`) rejects every change (409) while the header is present, before it reaches any service. So nothing is written to the store or the audit file, and each form shows its usual error. That covers statements as of a date, setting today, rates, claim actions and the rest. Loading a sheet is still allowed.

**Reading the sheet as it stood.** The people, claims, rates, settings and periods lists accept the header and return what stood at the end of that day. The rows, totals, header, periods panel, rates and summary are all worked out from those lists in the browser, so they follow automatically. This builds on the history the app already kept for statements as of a date, which only covered part of the data. A new migration, `V50__as_of_view.sql`, keeps the rest, each change dated with the sheet's today when it was made:
- the rest of each claim's state (number, opener, note, proofs, split-from, late entry);
- each person's name, terms and retirement;
- each period's state (added, closed, soft-closed, reopened, with its fixed totals);
- when statements were taken, patrons named and delegations made (a statement taken "as of" an earlier day still only counts from the day it was actually taken);
- each start or stop of watching;
- roles, permissions, period numbering and grace days.

**Limitations:**
- Changes made before this migration have no saved dates, so they show as they are now in every as-of view.
- A claim reassigned to another person keeps its current place in the list order, even when viewed as of an earlier date.
- Claim edit locks are not shown in the as-of view.

**One fix outside the as-of feature.** Scenario 2 failed on existing behaviour: after a refused "statement as of", the typed date stayed in the field, so the next plain statement reused it and was refused too. The field is now cleared after every statement attempt, refused or not (`people/people.ts`).
